                    "text": "MIT proved you can delete 90% of a neural network without losing accuracy.\nFive years later, nobody has implemented it.\n“The Lottery Ticket Hypothesis” just went from academic curiosity to production necessity, and it’s about to 10x your inference costs.\nHere’s what changed (and why this matters now):\nーーーー\nFollow @artificialintelligenceeee",
                    "id": "18110091955865918"
                }
            }
        ]
